body:
@coderabbitai Addressed in 09b0fcc5, keeping the source photograph unchanged.

`site_image_crop()` runs on `wp_ajax_crop-image` at priority 0, before `wp_ajax_crop_image()`, with the same `image_editor-<id>` nonce and `edit_post` checks. For a marked source with a current record, `crop_source()` makes a clean copy of the kept original in a temporary folder, under the attached file's name and at the attached file's size (EXIF-rotated and resized when the kept original is the pre-`-scaled`/`-rotated` one). `get_attached_file` returns that copy for the source ID only while `wp_crop_image()` runs. `wp_create_file_in_uploads`, which both the `site-icon` and default branches apply before `wp_copy_parent_attachment_properties()`, moves the crop next to the source and removes the filter and the temporary folder; a shutdown function removes it if the request ends earlier. Without a kept original, it logs `watermark_no_original` and shows the one-time notice.

Verified through real `admin-ajax.php` crop requests on `scripts/test-site.sh` (WordPress 7.1.3, PHP 8.3): 800px JPEG `custom_logo` crop and a 3000x2000 JPEG (`-scaled` 2560x1707) `site_icon` crop of the marked corner region both give clean crops (corner `0080ff`), while the sources stay marked (corner `fe0000`/`d80e1e`, records kept). The web container's `/tmp` is empty afterwards and `debug.log` has no plugin messages. `scripts/lint.sh php phpcs phpstan`: pass.

